    "abstract": {
      "confidence": "high",
      "page": 1,
      "text": "The Planckian relaxation rate ~/tP = 2πkBT sets a characteristic timescale for both the equilibration of quantum critical systems and maximal quantum chaos. In this note, we show that at the\ncritical coupling between a superconducting dot and the complex Sachdev-Ye-Kitaev model, known\nto be maximally chaotic, the pairing gap ∆ behaves as η ~/tP at low temperatures, where η is an\norder one constant. The lower critical temperature emerges with a further increase of the coupling\nstrength so that the finite ∆ domain is settled between the two critical temperatures."
    },
